{"entryId":"1584","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1584:1","sourceSha256":"e06e3efd34a578fc0a7f680adf37530d36afc9a910073e965fb2baec78c54fe9","englishSha256":"64292fbe702575b37ba24819f3b758593f9b34c679fdcc7671385172795641a5","citations":[{"id":"1584:1:citation-01","he":[0,15],"en":[7,14],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_7.8.1"},"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 7:8:1","assessment":"The reciprocal Dosa notice explicitly gives Dosa bar Tevet and Shir HaShirim Rabbah directly attests that form. The two witnesses differ between Nechunya and Chunya for the transmitter.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 897:1","target":{"entry":897,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 7:8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_7.8.1"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The Hebrew calls Dosa his son, as both the direct midrash and reciprocal Heilprin notice read. The old author note reverses that direction and is preserved in the baseline record.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 897:1","target":{"entry":897,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Shir HaShirim Rabbah 7:8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shir_HaShirim_Rabbah_7.8.1"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
